Found while closing k112. `perl maint/spec-drift-check.pl --from spec/v1.51.yaml --to spec/v1.55.yaml` reports a TYPE CHANGE:

  API::Docker::Type::Plugin::Config::Interface :: Types  array<object<PluginInterfaceType>> -> array<str>

v1.51 declares PluginInterfaceType as {Prefix, Capability, Version} (all required); v1.55 declares a string with example "docker.volumedriver/1.0". lib/API/Docker/Type/Plugin/Config/Interface.pm:15 has `docker types => [ 'PluginInterfaceType' ]`.

Suspicion, UNMEASURED: v1.55 corrects the spec, not the wire -- the daemon has always sent strings. Then `->types` is undef on every engine and the value sits in rejected_fields. There is no plugin fixture in t/fixtures/.

Measuring needs a plugin installed on an engine (a write, pulls from a registry) -- only with the maintainer's go-ahead. Read GET /plugins on Docker and Podman first; a machine that already has a plugin installed needs no write.

If confirmed: correcting a wrong type is not a rename, but it changes what an accessor returns -- decide per ADR 0001 (overlay, or a drift exception with WHY). Lanes: api-docker-engine-worker (measure), api-docker-type-writer (model).
